{"step_index":56,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T10:28:56Z","input_tokens":10883,"cache_read_tokens":167428,"output_tokens":1389,"thinking":"Creating the README, I need to outline installation, startup, testing, and usage for a Windows environment. Focus will be on clarity and completeness for the user, ensuring step-by-step instructions. Need to consider potential dependencies and common Windows-specific configurations.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# Code Flow Visualizer — Learn Coding Step by Step (No AI APIs)\n\nA complete, offline, local-first web application that teaches beginner programmers how Python code executes internally, one step at a time, using a **real execution-tracing engine** and a **deterministic rule-based explanation system** (zero AI APIs, zero API keys, and zero external cloud services).\n\n---\n\n## Features & Architecture\n\n1. **Separated Modular Architecture**:\n   - **Execution Engine ([engine.py](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/engine.py) & [engine.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/engine.js))**: AST syntax/support validator + step-by-step execution tracer recording snapshots of variables (`previous` vs `current`), loop iterations, condition evaluations (`left` op `right` $\\rightarrow$ `True`/`False`), function calls, and return values.\n   - **Rule-Based Teaching System ([explainer.py](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/explainer.py) & [explainer.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/explainer.js))**: Generates 7-part beginner and technical explanations, symbol definitions, practice prediction challenges, and answers to the 9 Built-In Code Questions from actual runtime state.\n   - **Interactive Workspace UI ([index.html](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/index.html), [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/styles.css), [app.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app.js))**:\n     - **Panel A (Code Editor — Left)**: Python syntax highlighting, line numbers, editable code, `Load Example`, `Edit Code`, `Reset`, `Analyze Code`, and distinct highlighting for Current (`▶`), Executed (`✓`), Next (`↳`), and Upcoming lines.\n     - **Panel B (Execution Visualizer — Center)**: Algorithm purpose & summary, step metrics, operation breakdown, condition/return outcome, Practice Mode prediction challenge, and interactive SVG Control Flow Graph.\n     - **Panel C (Variable Inspector & Built-In Questions — Right)**: Live variable table (`Variable | Previous | Current | Type | State`), visual list index strip (`nums[i]`), clickable variable history timeline, and 9 Built-In Code Questions.\n     - **Panel D (Beginner Explanation — Bottom)**: 7-part step-by-step mentor explanation with **Beginner Mode** and **Technical Mode**.\n\n2. **Preloaded Default Example — Maximum Subarray (`maxSubArray`)**:\n   - Preloaded with `class Solution: def maxSubArray(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:` and default input `nums = [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]` (expected output `6`, subarray `[4, -1, 2, 1]`).\n   - Includes one-click **Input Playground** presets for `[-5, -2, -8]` ($\\rightarrow$ `-2`), `[1, 2, 3, 4]` ($\\rightarrow$ `10`), `[7]` ($\\rightarrow$ `7`), and empty list `[]` validation.\n\n---\n\n## How to Run Locally on Windows\n\n### Option 1: Open Directly in Browser (Zero Setup)\nDouble-click [`index.html`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/index.html) or open it in any modern browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox). The client-side execution engine ([engine.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/engine.js)) and rule-based explainer ([explainer.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/explainer.js)) work 100% offline immediately.\n\n### Option 2: Run the Local Python Server (`sys.settrace` Backend)\nNo third-party `pip` packages are required (uses Python's standard library `ast`, `sys.settrace`, and `http.server`):\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\npython server.py\n```\n\nThen open **http://127.0.0.1:8080** in your browser.\n\n---\n\n## Running the Automated Tests\n\nTo verify the execution engine and rule-based explainer against all 12 required test cases (default `maxSubArray` $\\rightarrow$ `6`, all-negative `[-5, -2, -8]` $\\rightarrow$ `-2`, positive numbers, single-element, empty input, invalid syntax, unsupported constructs, infinite loop timeout, exceptions, snapshot navigation, and nested loops):\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\npython -m unittest test_engine.py -v\n```\n","Description":"Create README.md with complete architecture, Windows startup instructions, and testing commands","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\README.md","toolAction":"Creating documentation file README.md","toolSummary":"Create README.md with Windows setup and test instructions"}}]}
