{"step_index":60,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T10:39:48Z","input_tokens":5279,"cache_read_tokens":179817,"output_tokens":5470,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: tests failing with `NameError` inside `engine.py` point to an issue with how the `Solution` class is being accessed or defined within that scope. It's likely the `Solution` class isn't properly imported or is being referenced incorrectly in the `engine.py` context. Further investigation is needed to confirm the cause of the `NameError`.\n\n\nThe `NameError` within `engine.py` stems from `__build_class__` not being defined in the sandbox environment when a `class` is declared. Specifically, the `SUPPORTED_BUILTINS` dictionary lacks this crucial built-in function, and other exception classes like `object`, `Exception`, `IndexError`, `ValueError`, `TypeError` and `ZeroDivisionError` causing another series of `NameError` are missing. Adding `__build_class__` from `builtins`, and the object and exception class to this dictionary resolves the error and should allow the `class Solution` to be correctly executed.\n\n\nObserved a 404 error for `/favicon.ico`; will add explicit handling in the server to prevent the error message. The web UI appears functional at the specified address, displaying execution progress and a final result. Noted a UI issue: the flowchart's top nodes are clipped due to SVG container styling, requiring adjustment of the height or padding to improve display.\n\n\nThe immediate focus is on updating `engine.py` to include `__build_class__` within `SUPPORTED_BUILTINS` and ensure all the missing exception classes are present. The `write_to_file` function will be used to apply this necessary modification to the engine's internal environment. After updating `engine.py`, the system's integration with the web UI needs improvement, specifically, to make `/api/trace` and the execution timeline.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\nengine.py — Real Python Execution Tracing Engine & AST Support Checker\nNo AI APIs. Uses Python's `ast` module and `sys.settrace` in a restricted local namespace.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport ast\nimport builtins\nimport copy\nimport io\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nSUPPORTED_BUILTINS = {\n    \"__build_class__\": builtins.__build_class__,\n    \"__name__\": \"__main__\",\n    \"object\": object,\n    \"abs\": abs,\n    \"bool\": bool,\n    \"dict\": dict,\n    \"enumerate\": enumerate,\n    \"float\": float,\n    \"int\": int,\n    \"len\": len,\n    \"list\": list,\n    \"max\": max,\n    \"min\": min,\n    \"print\": print,\n    \"range\": range,\n    \"round\": round,\n    \"set\": set,\n    \"sorted\": sorted,\n    \"str\": str,\n    \"sum\": sum,\n    \"tuple\": tuple,\n    \"zip\": zip,\n    \"True\": True,\n    \"False\": False,\n    \"None\": None,\n    \"Exception\": Exception,\n    \"IndexError\": IndexError,\n    \"ValueError\": ValueError,\n    \"TypeError\": TypeError,\n    \"KeyError\": KeyError,\n    \"ZeroDivisionError\": ZeroDivisionError,\n}\n\nUNSUPPORTED_AST_NODES = {\n    ast.Import: \"Import statements (`import ...`) are not supported in the sandbox.\",\n    ast.ImportFrom: \"Import statements (`from ... import ...`) are not supported in the sandbox.\",\n    ast.AsyncFunctionDef: \"Async functions (`async def`) are not supported.\",\n    ast.Await: \"`await` expressions are not supported.\",\n    ast.AsyncFor: \"`async for` loops are not supported.\",\n    ast.AsyncWith: \"`async with` blocks are not supported.\",\n    ast.With: \"`with` context managers (such as file I/O) are not supported.\",\n    ast.Yield: \"Generators (`yield`) are not supported in the beginner tracer.\",\n    ast.YieldFrom: \"`yield from` is not supported.\",\n    ast.Lambda: \"`lambda` functions are not supported; please use a standard `def` function.\",\n    ast.Try: \"`try/except` blocks are not supported in basic mode.\",\n    ast.Global: \"`global` statements are not supported.\",\n    ast.Nonlocal: \"`nonlocal` statements are not supported.\",\n}\n\nFORBIDDEN_CALLS = {\n    \"eval\",\n    \"exec\",\n    \"open\",\n    \"compile\",\n    \"__import__\",\n    \"input\",\n    \"globals\",\n    \"locals\",\n    \"getattr\",\n    \"setattr\",\n    \"delattr\",\n}\n\n\ndef validate_python_support(source_code: str) -> Tuple[bool, Optional[str], Optional[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates syntax and checks whether the code uses only supported beginner constructs.\n    Returns (is_valid, error_message, line_number).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not source_code or not source_code.strip():\n        return False, \"Code editor is empty. Please enter a Python program.\", 1\n\n    try:\n        tree = ast.parse(source_code)\n    except SyntaxError as exc:\n        return False, f\"SyntaxError: {exc.msg}\", exc.lineno or 1\n\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        for node_type, msg in UNSUPPORTED_AST_NODES.items():\n            if isinstance(node, node_type):\n                return False, f\"Unsupported Construct: {msg}\", getattr(node, \"lineno\", 1)\n\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Call) and isinstance(node.func, ast.Name):\n            if node.func.id in FORBIDDEN_CALLS:\n                return (\n                    False,\n                    f\"Restricted Function: `{node.func.id}()` is disabled for security.\",\n                    getattr(node, \"lineno\", 1),\n                )\n\n    return True, None, None\n\n\ndef format_py_val(val: Any) -> str:\n    if isinstance(val, str):\n        return repr(val)\n    if isinstance(val, (int, float, bool, list, dict, tuple, set)) or val is None:\n        return repr(val)\n    return f\"<{type(val).__name__} instance>\"\n\n\ndef get_py_type(val: Any) -> str:\n    if val is None:\n        return \"NoneType\"\n    return type(val).__name__\n\n\ndef trace_python_program(\n    source_code: str,\n    custom_input_code: str = \"\",\n    max_steps: int = 400,\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Executes supported Python code step-by-step using `sys.settrace` and AST inspection.\n    If the code defines `class Solution:` with a method (like `maxSubArray`) and does not\n    invoke it at the bottom, automatically appends the invocation using `custom_input_code`.\n    \"\"\"\n    is_valid, err_msg, err_line = validate_python_support(source_code)\n    raw_lines = source_code.replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\").split(\"\\n\")\n\n    if not is_valid:\n        return {\n            \"ok\": False,\n            \"errorType\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n            \"errorMessage\": err_msg,\n            \"errorLine\": err_line,\n            \"rawLines\": raw_lines,\n            \"steps\": [],\n        }\n\n    # Check if custom_input_code has syntax errors\n    if custom_input_code.strip():\n        in_valid, in_err, in_line = validate_python_support(custom_input_code)\n        if not in_valid:\n            return {\n                \"ok\": False,\n                \"errorType\": \"INPUT_ERROR\",\n                \"errorMessage\": f\"Invalid Input Playground value: {in_err}\",\n                \"errorLine\": in_line,\n                \"rawLines\": raw_lines,\n                \"steps\": [],\n            }\n\n    full_code = source_code\n    has_solution_class = \"class Solution\" in source_code and \"def maxSubArray\" in source_code\n    has_explicit_call = (\n        \"Solution()\" in source_code\n        or \"maxSubArray(\" in source_code.split(\"def maxSubArray\")[-1]\n    )\n\n    if has_solution_class and not has_explicit_call:\n        input_line = custom_input_code.strip() or \"nums = [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]\"\n        full_code = (\n            source_code.rstrip()\n            + \"\\n\\n# --- Runner Invocation ---\\n\"\n            + input_line\n            + \"\\nresult = Solution().maxSubArray(nums)\\n\"\n        )\n        raw_lines = full_code.replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\").split(\"\\n\")\n\n    tree = ast.parse(full_code)\n    line_ast_map: Dict[int, ast.AST] = {}\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if hasattr(node, \"lineno\") and isinstance(\n            node,\n            (\n                ast.Assign,\n                ast.AugAssign,\n                ast.AnnAssign,\n                ast.If,\n                ast.For,\n                ast.While,\n                ast.Return,\n                ast.FunctionDef,\n                ast.ClassDef,\n                ast.Expr,\n                ast.Break,\n                ast.Continue,\n            ),\n        ):\n            if node.lineno not in line_ast_map:\n                line_ast_map[node.lineno] = node\n\n    steps: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n    stdout_buf = io.StringIO()\n    prev_vars_by_frame: Dict[int, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    loop_iter_counts: Dict[Tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n\n    def eval_in_frame(expr_node: ast.AST, frame) -> Any:\n        code_obj = compile(ast.Expression(expr_node), \"<expr>\", \"eval\")\n        return eval(code_obj, frame.f_globals, frame.f_locals)\n\n    def record_snapshot(frame, event: str, arg: Any):\n        if len(steps) >= max_steps:\n            raise TimeoutError(\n                f\"Execution exceeded maximum step limit ({max_steps} steps). Possible infinite loop.\"\n            )\n\n        lineno = frame.f_lineno\n        code_text = raw_lines[lineno - 1].strip() if 1 <= lineno <= len(raw_lines) else \"\"\n        if not code_text or code_text.startswith(\"#\"):\n            return\n\n        frame_id = id(frame)\n        func_name = frame.f_code.co_name\n        scope_title = \"Global Scope\" if func_name == \"<module>\" else f\"{func_name}()\"\n\n        prev_map = prev_vars_by_frame.setdefault(frame_id, {})\n        current_vars: Dict[str, Any] = {}\n        for k, v in frame.f_locals.items():\n            if k.startswith(\"__\") or k == \"self\" or k == \"Solution\":\n                continue\n            if callable(v) or isinstance(v, type):\n                continue\n            current_vars[k] = copy.deepcopy(v) if isinstance(v, (list, dict, set)) else v\n\n        stmt_node = line_ast_map.get(lineno)\n        condition_info = None\n        loop_info = None\n        operation_detail = None\n\n        if event == \"line\" and isinstance(stmt_node, ast.If):\n            try:\n                cond_val = bool(eval_in_frame(stmt_node.test, frame))\n                left_str, op_str, right_str = \"\", \"\", \"\"\n                if isinstance(stmt_node.test, ast.Compare) and len(stmt_node.test.ops) == 1:\n                    lval = eval_in_frame(stmt_node.test.left, frame)\n                    rval = eval_in_frame(stmt_node.test.comparators[0], frame)\n                    op_map = {\n                        ast.Eq: \"==\",\n                        ast.NotEq: \"!=\",\n                        ast.Lt: \"<\",\n                        ast.LtE: \"<=\",\n                        ast.Gt: \">\",\n                        ast.GtE: \">=\",\n                    }\n                    op_str = op_map.get(type(stmt_node.test.ops[0]), \"?\")\n                    left_str = format_py_val(lval)\n                    right_str = format_py_val(rval)\n                condition_info = {\n                    \"expr\": ast.unparse(stmt_node.test) if hasattr(ast, \"unparse\") else code_text,\n                    \"leftVal\": left_str,\n                    \"operator\": op_str,\n                    \"rightVal\": right_str,\n                    \"result\": cond_val,\n                }\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n\n        if event == \"line\" and isinstance(stmt_node, (ast.For, ast.While)):\n            key = (frame_id, lineno)\n            loop_iter_counts[key] = loop_iter_counts.get(key, 0) + 1\n            loop_info = {\n                \"loopType\": \"for\" if isinstance(stmt_node, ast.For) else \"while\",\n                \"iteration\": loop_iter_counts[key],\n            }\n\n        if event == \"line\" and isinstance(stmt_node, ast.AugAssign):\n            try:\n                target_name = stmt_node.target.id if isinstance(stmt_node.target, ast.Name) else \"var\"\n                before_v = current_vars.get(target_name)\n                rhs_v = eval_in_frame(stmt_node.value, frame)\n                op_char = (\n                    \"+\"\n                    if isinstance(stmt_node.op, ast.Add)\n                    else \"-\"\n                    if isinstance(stmt_node.op, ast.Sub)\n                    else \"*\"\n                )\n                operation_detail = {\n                    \"kind\": \"aug_assign\",\n                    \"target\": target_name,\n                    \"beforeVal\": format_py_val(before_v),\n                    \"rhsExpr\": ast.unparse(stmt_node.value) if hasattr(ast, \"unparse\") else \"\",\n                    \"rhsVal\": format_py_val(rhs_v),\n                    \"op\": op_char,\n                }\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n\n        var_inspector_rows = []\n        changed_vars = []\n        for k, v in current_vars.items():\n            curr_str = format_py_val(v)\n            if k not in prev_map:\n                status = \"created\"\n                prev_str = \"—\"\n                changed_vars.append({\"name\": k, \"prev\": \"—\", \"curr\": curr_str, \"status\": \"created\"})\n            elif format_py_val(prev_map[k]) != curr_str:\n                status = \"updated\"\n                prev_str = format_py_val(prev_map[k])\n                changed_vars.append({\"name\": k, \"prev\": prev_str, \"curr\": curr_str, \"status\": \"updated\"})\n            else:\n                status = \"unchanged\"\n                prev_str = curr_str\n\n            var_inspector_rows.append(\n                {\n                    \"name\": k,\n                    \"previous\": prev_str,\n                    \"current\": curr_str,\n                    \"rawValue\": v if isinstance(v, (int, float, bool, str, list)) else curr_str,\n                    \"type\": get_py_type(v),\n                    \"status\": status,\n                }\n            )\n\n        prev_vars_by_frame[frame_id] = copy.deepcopy(current_vars)\n\n        steps.append(\n            {\n                \"stepIndex\": len(steps) + 1,\n                \"event\": event,\n                \"line\": lineno,\n                \"codeText\": code_text,\n                \"functionName\": scope_title,\n                \"variables\": var_inspector_rows,\n                \"changedVars\": changed_vars,\n                \"condition\": condition_info,\n                \"loop\": loop_info,\n                \"operationDetail\": operation_detail,\n                \"returnValue\": format_py_val(arg) if event == \"return\" else None,\n                \"stdout\": stdout_buf.getvalue().splitlines(),\n            }\n        )\n\n    def trace_dispatch(frame, event, arg):\n        if frame.f_code.co_filename != \"<user_code>\":\n            return trace_dispatch\n        if event in (\"line\", \"call\", \"return\"):\n            record_snapshot(frame, event, arg)\n        return trace_dispatch\n\n    compiled = compile(full_code, \"<user_code>\", \"exec\")\n    sandbox_globals = {\"__builtins__\": SUPPORTED_BUILTINS, \"__name__\": \"__main__\"}\n    old_stdout = sys.stdout\n    error_info = None\n\n    try:\n        sys.stdout = stdout_buf\n        sys.settrace(trace_dispatch)\n        exec(compiled, sandbox_globals)\n    except Exception as exc:\n        tb = sys.exc_info()[2]\n        err_ln = 1\n        while tb is not None:\n            if tb.tb_frame.f_code.co_filename == \"<user_code>\":\n                err_ln = tb.tb_lineno\n            tb = tb.tb_next\n        error_info = {\n            \"type\": type(exc).__name__,\n            \"message\": str(exc),\n            \"line\": err_ln,\n        }\n    finally:\n        sys.settrace(None)\n        sys.stdout = old_stdout\n\n    aligned_steps = _align_post_execution_variables(steps)\n\n    return {\n        \"ok\": error_info is None,\n        \"error\": error_info,\n        \"rawLines\": raw_lines,\n        \"steps\": aligned_steps,\n        \"finalResult\": format_py_val(sandbox_globals.get(\"result\")) if \"result\" in sandbox_globals else None,\n    }\n\n\ndef _align_post_execution_variables(raw_steps: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    if not raw_steps:\n        return []\n\n    aligned = []\n    for i, step in enumerate(raw_steps):\n        step_copy = copy.deepcopy(step)\n        before_vars = {v[\"name\"]: v[\"current\"] for v in step[\"variables\"]}\n\n        after_vars_list = step[\"variables\"]\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(raw_steps)):\n            if raw_steps[j][\"functionName\"] == step[\"functionName\"]:\n                after_vars_list = raw_steps[j][\"variables\"]\n                break\n\n        recomputed_vars = []\n        changed_summary = []\n        for v in after_vars_list:\n            name = v[\"name\"]\n            curr_val = v[\"current\"]\n            if name not in before_vars:\n                status = \"created\"\n                prev_val = \"—\"\n                changed_summary.append(f\"{name}: (created) -> {curr_val}\")\n            elif before_vars[name] != curr_val:\n                status = \"updated\"\n                prev_val = before_vars[name]\n                changed_summary.append(f\"{name}: {prev_val} -> {curr_val}\")\n            else:\n                status = \"unchanged\"\n                prev_val = curr_val\n\n            recomputed_vars.append(\n                {\n                    \"name\": name,\n                    \"previous\": prev_val,\n                    \"current\": curr_val,\n                    \"rawValue\": v[\"rawValue\"],\n                    \"type\": v[\"type\"],\n                    \"status\": status,\n                }\n            )\n\n        step_copy[\"beforeVars\"] = before_vars\n        step_copy[\"variables\"] = recomputed_vars\n        step_copy[\"changedSummary\"] = (\n            \", \".join(changed_summary) if changed_summary else \"No variable values changed\"\n        )\n        step_copy[\"nextLine\"] = raw_steps[i + 1][\"line\"] if i + 1 < len(raw_steps) else None\n        aligned.append(step_copy)\n\n    return aligned\n","Description":"Fix SUPPORTED_BUILTINS in engine.py by adding builtins.__build_class__ so class Solution definitions execute properly in sandboxed exec()","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\engine.py","toolAction":"Fixing __build_class__ in engine.py","toolSummary":"Add __build_class__ to SUPPORTED_BUILTINS in engine.py"}}]}
